ject array) {\n  2182\t        return array != null ? Array.getLength(array) : 0;\n  2183\t    }\n  2184\t\n  2185\t    /**\n  2186\t     * Gets a hash code for an array handling multidimensional arrays.\n  2187\t     * <p>\n  2188\t     * Multi-dimensional primitive arrays are also handled by this method.\n  2189\t     * </p>\n  2190\t     *\n  2191\t     * @param array  the array to get a hash code for, may be {@code null}.\n  2192\t     * @return a hash code for the array.\n  2193\t     * @see HashCodeBuilder\n  2194\t     */\n  2195\t    public static int hashCode(final Object array) {\n  2196\t        return new HashCodeBuilder().append(array).toHashCode();\n  2197\t    }\n  2198\t\n  2199\t    static <K> void increment(final Map<K, MutableInt> occurrences, final K boxed) {\n  2200\t        occurrences.computeIfAbsent(boxed, k -> new MutableInt()).increment();\n  2201\t    }\n  2202\t\n  2203\t    /**\n  2204\t     * Finds the indices of the given value in the array.\n  2205\t     * <p>\n  2206\t     * This method returns an empty BitSet for a {@code null} input array.\n  2207\t     * </p>\n  2208\t     *\n  2209\t     * @param array  the array to search for the object, may be {@code null}.\n  2210\t     * @param valueToFind  the value to find.\n  2211\t     * @return a BitSet of all the indices of the value within the array,\n  2212\t     *  an empty BitSet if not found or {@code null} array input.\n  2213\t     * @since 3.10\n  2214\t     */\n  2215\t    public static BitSet indexesOf(final boolean[] array, final boolean valueToFind) {\n  2216\t        return indexesOf(array, valueToFind, 0);\n  2217\t    }\n  2218\t\n  2219\t    /**\n  2220\t     * Finds the indices of the given value in the array starting at the given index.\n  2221\t     * <p>\n  2222\t     * This method returns an empty BitSet for a {@code null} input array.\n  2223\t     * </p>\n  2224\t     * <p>\n  2225\t     * A negative startIndex is treated as zero. A startIndex larger than the arra